WELCOME_START=Start writing
WELCOME_1_TITLE=Welcome to Arabic Learn!
WELCOME_1=Write Arabic by hand, the way it is written: Arabic Learn! shows every letter’s strokes in order, from right to left, in each of the forms it takes in a word, reads what you write and tells you how well it went. It works offline, and everything stays on this device.
WELCOME_PHONE=Arabic Learn! is designed for tablets. It works on phones too, with less room to write.
WELCOME_2_TITLE=Pencil or finger
WELCOME_2_TITLE_ANDROID=Stylus or finger
WELCOME_2=Write with the Apple Pencil — fingers then move the page — or, with the hand on the bar, with one finger, and move the page with two. Arabic Learn! switches by itself when the Pencil writes. The tools are on a bar you can drag anywhere; a double tap on its handle folds it away.
WELCOME_2_ANDROID=Write with a stylus — fingers then move the page — or, with the hand on the bar, with one finger, and move the page with two. Arabic Learn! switches by itself when the stylus writes. The tools are on a bar you can drag anywhere; a double tap on its handle folds it away.
WELCOME_3_TITLE=Scan pages
WELCOME_3=In Lectures, Scan pages turns a book or a worksheet into pages to write on with the camera, and From Photos makes a PDF of pictures you already have. Write over them, mark them and keep them with your canvases.
WELCOME_4_TITLE=Copy, paste, check
WELCOME_4=Draw around writing with the lasso: copy it, Copy as text to use it in any app, Check what it says, or Save word. Press and hold the page to paste: Paste text writes text copied anywhere as handwriting, stroke by stroke.
WELCOME_5_TITLE=Translate
WELCOME_5=Lasso your writing and choose Translate with Google to read it in your language. In Vocabulary, Translate with Google goes the other way: type in your language and get it in Arabic, with its words to save, practise or write. The translation models download once, then work offline.
WELCOME_6_TITLE=Learn
WELCOME_6=The menu at the top left has everything to study: the Arabic alphabet with each letter’s joined forms, the letters with their stroke order, words to read and listen to, practice, reviews and exams. Lectures has free lessons, and the PDFs, photos and pages you scan, to read and write on.
WELCOME_7_TITLE=Your progress
WELCOME_7=Statistics shows your streak, the days you wrote, your scores week by week, your exams and the characters that need more work; the Album keeps every character you practised, with each try. It all stays on this device: Settings › Your data makes a backup.
LECTURE_PHRASEBOOK=Arabic phrasebook
LECTURE_PHRASEBOOK_ABOUT=Arabic, its alphabet and pronunciation, a little grammar, and the phrases a trip needs (greetings, numbers, time, getting around, eating, shopping), with their romanization. From Wikivoyage.

